{
  "note": "Stop the review-slider arrows appearing on every multi-block media-with-text section on the site. Only the html setting of sections/footer-group.json -> brand_layout_css changes; the whole value is carried here verbatim so the diff is auditable and the push is a straight replacement.",
  "the_bug": "The arrow-injection script guarded on `items.length < 2`, but the CSS that actually makes a media-with-text scroll horizontally is scoped to `:has(> .media-with-text__item:nth-child(6))`. JS said 2, CSS said 6. Arrows were injected on any section with 2+ blocks, and pinned permanently visible by the always-visible rule, onto sections that were never turned into scrollers - so clicking them did nothing at all.",
